 "standard_url": "https://tea.texas.gov/about-tea/laws-and-rules/sboe-rules-tac/sboe-tac-currently-in-effect/ch111c.pdf",
 "standard_text": "A.5A solve linear equations in one variable, including those for which the application of the distributive property is necessary and for which variables are included on both sides",
 "meta_desc": "Free Algebra I worksheets for Texas TEKS A.5A: solve multi-step linear equations with distributing, variables on both sides, fractions, decimals and word problems. 100 questions with answers.",
 "key_big": "Distribute, combine, then isolate the variable.",
 "key_sub": "3(x − 4) + 2 = 5x − 16 gives x = 3.",
 "body_html": "<h2>How to think about it</h2><ul><li>Distribute and combine like terms on each side.</li><li>Get the variable terms on one side and the numbers on the other.</li><li>Clear fractions by multiplying <b>every term</b> by the common denominator.</li><li>Check by putting your answer back in.</li></ul><h2>Examples</h2><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>3(<i>x</i> − 4) + 2 = 5<i>x</i> − 16</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>3<i>x</i> − 10 = 5<i>x</i> − 16</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>6 = 2<i>x</i></p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: <i>x</i> = 3</p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><div class='sn-tw'><table class='sn-table'><thead><tr><th>Mistake</th><th>What to do instead</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Distributing to only the first term</td><td>3(<i>x</i> − 4) = 3<i>x</i> − 12.</td></tr><tr><td>Moving a term without changing its sign</td><td>Subtract from both sides.</td></tr><tr><td>Clearing only one side</td><td>Multiply every term.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
 "faq": [
  {
   "q": "What does TEKS A.5A ask?",
   "a": "Solve linear equations in one variable, including those for which the application of the distributive property is necessary and for which variables are included on both sides."
  },
  {
   "q": "What if the variables cancel?",
   "a": "A true statement means all numbers; a false one means no solution."
  },
  {
   "q": "How do I clear decimals?",
   "a": "Multiply every term by 10 or 100."
  },
  {
   "q": "Why check?",
   "a": "It catches sign mistakes."
  }
 ],
